{
 "artist": "John Singer Sargent",
 "slug": "john-singer-sargent",
 "born": 1856,
 "died": 1925,
 "nationality": "American",
 "facts": [
  {
   "text": "In 1878, the year he first showed at the Paris Salon, Sargent signed En route pour la pêche in capitals: 'JOHN S. SARGENT. / PARIS 1878'.",
   "source": "https://www.nga.gov/collection/art-object-page.166472.html",
   "source_name": "National Gallery of Art"
  },
  {
   "text": "From about 1879 his usual signature in oil is a cursive 'John S. Sargent', often with the year and sometimes the place, as in 'John S. Sargent / Ronjoux 1879'.",
   "source": "https://www.nga.gov/collection/art-object-page.97063.html",
   "source_name": "National Gallery of Art"
  },
  {
   "text": "Several of his full-length portraits split the signature and the date between the two upper corners, for example 'John S. Sargent' upper left and '1888' upper right on the portrait of Eleanora Iselin.",
   "source": "https://www.nga.gov/collection/art-object-page.50217.html",
   "source_name": "National Gallery of Art"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sargent often gave portraits and sketches as gifts with a dedication: Miss Beatrice Townsend (1882) is inscribed 'to my friend Mrs Townsend / John S. Sargent', for the sitter's mother.",
   "source": "https://www.nga.gov/collection/art-object-page.96999.html",
   "source_name": "National Gallery of Art"
  },
  {
   "text": "Many of his early sketchbook drawings carry a number such as 'J.S.238' added later; the National Gallery catalogues these as written by an unknown hand, not as his signature.",
   "source": "https://www.nga.gov/collection/art-object-page.184302.html",
   "source_name": "National Gallery of Art"
  }
 ],
